// ─── ⛔ #nova-does-not-find-the-game — WHERE THE GAME IS, ASKED OF EVERY PLACE THAT RECORDS IT ─────────────────────────────
// A modder on Discord (2026-11-02): Nova does not find their Hearts of Iron IV folder. It asked ONE place, the Uninstall key
// Steam writes for app 394360, through reg.exe and in the 64-bit view only, then five fixed folders; and when none of them held
// the game it carried on with the first as if it did. Every maker was then missing the base game with nothing to say why, and
// a modder had no way to say where the game is: the .env reader reads __dirname, which in the packaged exe is inside app.asar.
// Measured on the owner's machine 2026-11-03: Steam wrote that key in the 64-bit view only, and Valve\Steam InstallPath in both;
// on another machine any of them can be missing, and a game in G:\Games\Steam\…, or in any library Steam was told about, is in
// none of the five folders. Steam's own record of where its libraries are is libraryfolders.vdf, and of where a game is in one,
// that library's appmanifest_394360.acf.
//
// ⚠️ AND reg.exe WRITES A PIPE IN THE CONSOLE'S OEM CODE PAGE, which the old reader decoded as UTF-8. Measured (OEMCP 437) on two
// values this machine already has: U+00B5 came as the byte E6 and decoded to U+FFFD, and U+00AE, which CP437 has not got, came
// as a best-fit "r" — ASCII, and wrong. So a Steam folder under D:\Игры or C:\Users\José never matched the disk. `reg export`
// writes UTF-16 and is exact for both; readRegistryPath asks it only when reg query's answer is not plain ASCII or names nothing
// that exists. Measured: reg query 10–28 ms, reg export 25–34 ms, PowerShell 211 ms.
const HOI4_STEAM_APP_ID = "394360";
// What makes a folder the game's is mod-index.js isHoi4GameFolder: hoi4.exe, or the Linux (hoi4 + run_hoi4) or Mac (hoi4.app)
// program — a native Linux install seen through Wine has no hoi4.exe. The name below is what Nova's messages say to look for.
const HOI4_GAME_EXE = "hoi4.exe";
const DEFAULT_WORKSHOP_ROOT = "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Steam\\steamapps\\workshop\\content\\394360";
// The game folder detection found: "" when no folder holding hoi4.exe was found anywhere. resolveHoi4GameRoot asks the
// modder's choice and HOI4_ROOT before it on every call, and answers NO_GAME_FOLDER rather than a folder that was not there.
let GAME_ROOT = "";
let WORKSHOP_ROOT = DEFAULT_WORKSHOP_ROOT;   // the Workshop folder of the library that holds the game, once one does
// What every caller of resolveHoi4GameRoot gets when there is no game: a folder that never exists, in Nova's own app data, so
// each of the ~200 callers reads nothing from it, exactly as each read from the missing default folder before — never "",
// which path.resolve turns into the current folder, and never a guessed Steam folder that may hold an uninstall's leftovers.
// Nothing shows it: /api/root, /api/about and the Home page say "not found" instead (gameFolderReport).
const NO_GAME_FOLDER = path.join(NOVA_APP_DATA_DIR, "no-game-folder");
// HOI4 authors interface at a 1920×1080 base; GUI percentages (e.g. a gridbox at x = -11%) resolve against
// the parent container width/height, which for tech folders is 100% of this base. Used to turn % origins
// into pixels so percentage-positioned chains land where the engine draws them. #gridbox-pct
const GUI_REF_W = 1920, GUI_REF_H = 1080;

